# ffi/logs/rust/stage3-M3.log
# W3 stage 3 part 3: M3 (Probe in ListProbeResponse) over P3.1.
# A oneof of five members including a payload-free one, and three optional scalars.
# Both shapes are UNMEASURED ON .NET, so these rows will be read across by the C# slice.
# 2026-09-18
#
# CONFIGURATION (R7)
#   machine        4 vCPU Intel Xeon @ 2.80GHz, 15 GB, Ubuntu 24.04.4, Linux 6.18.44 x86_64,
#                  container. No CPU pinning, no governor control.
#   rust           rustc/cargo 1.94.1, release. MSRV 1.88 declared, NOT verified.
#   incumbent      prost 0.14.4
#   LINKAGE        cdylib (libak_core.so), dynamic linker. Not a static link.
#   guard          on
#   content set    ascii
#   class          M3 is a REAL shape by design/SHAPES.md: invented as a message, but
#                  both of its shapes are real, and the schema has 19 oneofs in 413
#                  fields. It is NOT a control. M6 and M7 are the controls and are not
#                  built yet.
#
# WHAT M3 IS FOR, AND WHAT IT IS NOT
#   It is shape coverage, not a timing table. One payload, one timing row set, and the
#   substance in section 2b. Kept small deliberately.
#
# THE GROUP LAYOUT CHOSEN FOR A ONEOF, AND THE ALTERNATIVE NOT MEASURED
#   A oneof becomes a <name>_case discriminant carrying the ACTIVE MEMBER'S TAG, plus
#   every member inlined beside it. Not a union: ABI v1 section 6 says a group needs a
#   fixed shape and not a size bound, and a union makes the layout depend on which
#   member is largest, which a host reproducing offsets by hand can get wrong silently.
#   The cost is the size of the group. A union is an unmeasured alternative and is
#   recorded as one rather than assumed equivalent.
#
#   A <name>_case the codec does not recognise is refused with AK_ERR_ABI rather than
#   encoded as nothing: a host generated against a newer descriptor is exactly the skew
#   that must be loud. That path is not exercised by any vector here, because nothing
#   in this build can produce an unknown case; it is stated as built, not as measured.
#
# HAZARDS (R9)
#   - The unknown-field vectors in section 2b are HAND-BUILT wire with no manifest hash.
#     A corpus generated from the schema that reads it cannot contain a field the reader
#     does not know, which is README section 10 item 1 and the reason they are built
#     here. Their check is agreement of all four arms on the decoded value AND on the
#     re-encoded bytes, with prost as the fourth, independent opinion.
#   - P3.1 is 12 KB and 200 elements; its timing rows are a mid-size figure, and the
#     run-to-run spread is the figure, not the median.

